ersion\":\"ceiba-exact-result-receipt-v1\",\"source_id\":null,\"source_ids\":[\"MOSAIC\",\"NEXUS\"],\"source_path\":null,\"source_sha256\":null,\"source_size_bytes\":null,\"total_source_bytes\":8078}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n{\"action\":\"reopen_exact\",\"result_id\":\"RESULT-001\"}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n{\"object_id\":\"result:RESULT-001\",\"object_version\":\"58d3d2717469174d7313108815f4c33d7b2b8d28dcf690f6e964c8ad23db7386\",\"result_id\":\"RESULT-016\",\"result_kind\":\"exact_reopen_observation\",\"schema\":\"ceiba-action-result-v1\"}\n--- exact result body ---\n{\"original_result_id\":\"RESULT-001\",\"original_sha256\":\"58d3d2717469174d7313108815f4c33d7b2b8d28dcf690f6e964c8ad23db7386\",\"schema\":\"architecture-exact-reopen-v0\"}\n--- exact original model-visible result ---\n{\"object_id\":\"batch:AURORA:1-64+BASTION:1-64\",\"object_version\":\"d40538a3737a4f373b7eabc2e3a41e0637476655cf7441bd9c309545cffc2f71\",\"result_id\":\"RESULT-001\",\"result_kind\":\"source_observation\",\"schema\":\"ceiba-action-result-v1\"}\n--- exact result body ---\n{\"schema\":\"architecture-batch-observation-v0\",\"segments\":[{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"AURORA\",\"start_line\":1},{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"BASTION\",\"start_line\":1}],\"total_source_bytes\":8057}\n--- exact batch segment 1 ---\n{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"AURORA\",\"source_path\":\"sources/AURORA_AUTHORITY.md\",\"source_sha256\":\"debbe3de17dc0511fe3b9f5be920a83367c84efaedb34ef4095a9add315a0761\",\"source_size_bytes\":4111,\"start_line\":1}\n--- exact source range ---\n# Emergency authority and restoration accountability\n\n## Frozen findings\n\nThe incident commander may isolate zones and order emergency work. Only the county health officer may lift a do-not-drink order, and only after current laboratory and distribution-system verification; a utility repair or green mechanical check is not public-health authorization.\nEmergency procurement does not waive operator certification, chain of custody, environmental permits, access control, or fiscal review. Final closure requires the utility director to accept every declared blocker and residual risk.\nA handoff is valid only when the receiving lead acknowledges the same hydraulic model, treatment train, sampling plan, pump configuration, and communication version. A version mismatch blocks closure.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nBASTION and CIPHER supply hydraulic and laboratory evidence but cannot lift health restrictions. NEXUS supplies independent readiness findings but does not execute restoration.\nMOSAIC owns rollback mechanics; AURORA preserves separation among detection, recommendation, authorization, execution, verification, communication, and closure.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | asset/zone | version | measure | unit | status |\n|---|---|---|---:|---|---|\n| AUT-000 | incident-command | v2 | 1.0 | approval | superseded |\n| AUT-001 | health-officer | v2 | 2.3 | approval | current |\n| AUT-002 | utility-director | v2 | 3.6 | approval | current |\n| AUT-003 | public-information | v2 | 1.8 | approval | current |\n| AUT-004 | incident-command | v2 | 3.1 | approval | current |\n| AUT-005 | health-officer | v2 | 1.3 | approval | current |\n| AUT-006 | utility-director | v2 | 2.6 | approval | current |\n| AUT-007 | public-information | v2 | 3.9 | approval | current |\n| AUT-008 | incident-command | v2 | 2.1 | approval | current |\n| AUT-009 | health-officer | v2 | 3.4 | approval | current |\n| AUT-010 | utility-director | v2 | 1.6 | approval | current |\n| AUT-011 | public-information | v2 | 2.9 | approval | current |\n| AUT-012 | incident-command | v2 | 1.1 | approval | current |\n| AUT-013 | health-officer | v2 | 2.4 | approval | current |\n| AUT-014 | utility-director | v3 | 3.7 | approval | current |\n| AUT-015 | public-information | v3 | 1.9 | approval | current |\n| AUT-016 | incident-command | v3 | 3.2 | approval | current |\n| AUT-017 | health-officer | v3 | 1.4 | approval | current |\n| AUT-018 | utility-director | v3 | 2.7 | approval | current |\n| AUT-019 | public-information | v3 | 4.0 | approval | superseded |\n| AUT-020 | incident-command | v3 | 2.2 | approval | current |\n| AUT-021 | health-officer | v3 | 3.5 | approval | current |\n| AUT-022 | utility-director | v3 | 1.7 | approval | current |\n| AUT-023 | public-information | v3 | 3.0 | approval | current |\n| AUT-024 | incident-command | v3 | 1.2 | approval | current |\n| AUT-025 | health-officer | v3 | 2.5 | approval | current |\n| AUT-026 | utility-director | v3 | 3.8 | approval | current |\n| AUT-027 | public-information | v3 | 2.0 | approval | current |\n| AUT-028 | incident-command | v4 | 3.3 | approval | current |\n| AUT-029 | health-officer | v4 | 1.5 | approval | current |\n| AUT-030 | utility-director | v4 | 2.8 | approval | current |\n| AUT-031 | public-information | v4 | 1.0 | approval | current |\n| AUT-032 | incident-command | v4 | 2.3 | approval | current |\n| AUT-033 | health-officer | v4 | 3.6 | approval | current |\n| AUT-034 | utility-director | v4 | 1.8 | approval | current |\n| AUT-035 | public-information | v4 | 3.1 | approval | current |\n| AUT-036 | incident-command | v4 | 1.3 | approval | current |\n| AUT-037 | health-officer | v4 | 2.6 | approval | current |\n| AUT-038 | utility-director | v4 | 3.9 | approval | superseded |\n| AUT-039 | public-information | v4 | 2.1 | approval | current |\n| AUT-040 | incident-command | v4 | 3.4 | approval | current |\n| AUT-041 | health-officer | v4 | 1.6 | approval | current |\n\n## Decision constraints\n\nName who may isolate, repair, verify, reopen service, lift advisories, and close.\nTreat semantic records and candidate mutations as non-authoritative work products.\n--- exact batch segment 2 ---\n{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"BASTION\",\"source_path\":\"sources/BASTION_HYDRAULICS.md\",\"source_sha256\":\"f0a85d8273e5058984554a6383d51616f2e103f141b7e268f67215b90fc7ed60\",\"source_size_bytes\":3483,\"start_line\":1}\n--- exact source range ---\n# Hydraulic pressure, storage, and zone isolation evidence\n\n## Frozen findings\n\nCurrent minimum distribution pressure is 42 psi in the north zone. The restoration gate is at least 35 psi at every critical node for three consecutive thirty-minute windows; 42 psi must not be converted to 42 kPa or treated as proof of water quality.\nRidge storage contains 5.8 million gallons, while the twelve-hour emergency reserve is 3.2 million gallons. Stored volume and usable treated reserve are different controls.\nA valve map, pump curve, demand allocation, or zone-boundary change makes earlier pressure and residence-time checks stale for the changed candidate.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nDELTA pump sequencing depends on BASTION pressure and ECHO power. CIPHER sampling locations must follow the current BASTION flow paths.\nMOSAIC rollback is allowed only while the prior valve map remains valid and a current BASTION pressure check passes for the rollback candidate.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | asset/zone | version | measure | unit | status |\n|---|---|---|---:|---|---|\n| HYD-000 | north-zone | v2 | 42.0 | psi | superseded |\n| HYD-001 | south-zone | v2 | 43.3 | psi | current |\n| HYD-002 | ridge-tank | v2 | 44.6 | psi | current |\n| HYD-003 | valve-grid | v2 | 42.8 | psi | current |\n| HYD-004 | north-zone | v2 | 44.1 | psi | current |\n| HYD-005 | south-zone | v2 | 42.3 | psi | current |\n| HYD-006 | ridge-tank | v2 | 43.6 | psi | current |\n| HYD-007 | valve-grid | v2 | 44.9 | psi | current |\n| HYD-008 | north-zone | v2 | 43.1 | psi | current |\n| HYD-009 | south-zone | v2 | 44.4 | psi | current |\n| HYD-010 | ridge-tank | v2 | 42.6 | psi | current |\n| HYD-011 | valve-grid | v2 | 43.9 | psi | current |\n| HYD-012 | north-zone | v2 | 42.1 | psi | current |\n| HYD-013 | south-zone | v2 | 43.4 | psi | current |\n| HYD-014 | ridge-tank | v3 | 44.7 | psi | current |\n| HYD-015 | valve-grid | v3 | 42.9 | psi | current |\n| HYD-016 | north-zone | v3 | 44.2 | psi | current |\n| HYD-017 | south-zone | v3 | 42.4 | psi | current |\n| HYD-018 | ridge-tank | v3 | 43.7 | psi | current |\n| HYD-019 | valve-grid | v3 | 45.0 | psi | superseded |\n| HYD-020 | north-zone | v3 | 43.2 | psi | current |\n| HYD-021 | south-zone | v3 | 44.5 | psi | current |\n| HYD-022 | ridge-tank | v3 | 42.7 | psi | current |\n| HYD-023 | valve-grid | v3 | 44.0 | psi | current |\n| HYD-024 | north-zone | v3 | 42.2 | psi | current |\n| HYD-025 | south-zone | v3 | 43.5 | psi | current |\n| HYD-026 | ridge-tank | v3 | 44.8 | psi | current |\n| HYD-027 | valve-grid | v3 | 43.0 | psi | current |\n| HYD-028 | north-zone | v4 | 44.3 | psi | current |\n| HYD-029 | south-zone | v4 | 42.5 | psi | current |\n| HYD-030 | ridge-tank | v4 | 43.8 | psi | current |\n| HYD-031 | valve-grid | v4 | 42.0 | psi | current |\n| HYD-032 | north-zone | v4 | 43.3 | psi | current |\n| HYD-033 | south-zone | v4 | 44.6 | psi | current |\n| HYD-034 | ridge-tank | v4 | 42.8 | psi | current |\n| HYD-035 | valve-grid | v4 | 44.1 | psi | current |\n| HYD-036 | north-zone | v4 | 42.3 | psi | current |\n| HYD-037 | south-zone | v4 | 43.6 | psi | current |\n| HYD-038 | ridge-tank | v4 | 44.9 | psi | superseded |\n| HYD-039 | valve-grid | v4 | 43.1 | psi | current |\n| HYD-040 | north-zone | v4 | 44.4 | psi | current |\n| HYD-041 | south-zone | v4 | 42.6 | psi | current |\n\n## Decision constraints\n\nPreserve psi, gallons, the three-window rule, and candidate currency.\nDistinguish hydraulic service from microbiological and chemical clearance.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n{\"action\":\"reopen_exact\",\"result_id\":\"RESULT-002\"}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n{\"object_id\":\"result:RESULT-002\",\"object_version\":\"ff48adcd9a8685c9568506e43f953213d7d1728c2b4ca22b125cbc7d3e0dbcc7\",\"result_id\":\"RESULT-017\",\"result_kind\":\"exact_reopen_observation\",\"schema\":\"ceiba-action-result-v1\"}\n--- exact result body ---\n{\"original_result_id\":\"RESULT-002\",\"original_sha256\":\"ff48adcd9a8685c9568506e43f953213d7d1728c2b4ca22b125cbc7d3e0dbcc7\",\"schema\":\"architecture-exact-reopen-v0\"}\n--- exact original model-visible result ---\n{\"object_id\":\"batch:CIPHER:1-64+DELTA:1-64\",\"object_version\":\"64721c48b86decba9adecca404e0e207db15cc1c0611470f2fe6e28207610bef\",\"result_id\":\"RESULT-002\",\"result_kind\":\"source_observation\",\"schema\":\"ceiba-action-result-v1\"}\n--- exact result body ---\n{\"schema\":\"architecture-batch-observation-v0\",\"segments\":[{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"CIPHER\",\"start_line\":1},{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"DELTA\",\"start_line\":1}],\"total_source_bytes\":8452}\n--- exact batch segment 1 ---\n{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"CIPHER\",\"source_path\":\"sources/CIPHER_LAB.md\",\"source_sha256\":\"6db7f6a91d666ab9e013e147aa946885080f48117bd461c8a542171378aba4cb\",\"source_size_bytes\":3991,\"start_line\":1}\n--- exact source range ---\n# Laboratory sampling, detection limits, and clearance evidence\n\n## Frozen findings\n\nThe current confirmatory set has zero E. coli positives across forty-eight samples. Clearance requires two complete rounds at least sixteen hours apart; one clean round is insufficient.\nThe benzene reporting limit is 0.5 micrograms per liter and the action threshold is 5.0 micrograms per liter. The reporting limit is not the action threshold and neither is a percent concentration.\nA flow-path, disinfectant-dose, source-water, sampling-plan, or laboratory-method change makes prior samples stale for the changed candidate.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nCIPHER sample placement consumes BASTION flow paths and GARNET contamination hypotheses. HELIX governs chain of custody and laboratory access.\nAURORA consumes current CIPHER findings for advisory decisions; CIPHER does not itself authorize public restoration.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | asset/zone | version | measure | unit | status |\n|---|---|---|---:|---|---|\n| LAB-000 | entry-point | v2 | 0.0 | positive-samples | superseded |\n| LAB-001 | north-grid | v2 | 1.3 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-002 | south-grid | v2 | 2.6 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-003 | hospital-loop | v2 | 0.8 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-004 | entry-point | v2 | 2.1 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-005 | north-grid | v2 | 0.3 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-006 | south-grid | v2 | 1.6 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-007 | hospital-loop | v2 | 2.9 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-008 | entry-point | v2 | 1.1 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-009 | north-grid | v2 | 2.4 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-010 | south-grid | v2 | 0.6 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-011 | hospital-loop | v2 | 1.9 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-012 | entry-point | v2 | 0.1 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-013 | north-grid | v2 | 1.4 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-014 | south-grid | v3 | 2.7 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-015 | hospital-loop | v3 | 0.9 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-016 | entry-point | v3 | 2.2 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-017 | north-grid | v3 | 0.4 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-018 | south-grid | v3 | 1.7 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-019 | hospital-loop | v3 | 3.0 | positive-samples | superseded |\n| LAB-020 | entry-point | v3 | 1.2 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-021 | north-grid | v3 | 2.5 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-022 | south-grid | v3 | 0.7 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-023 | hospital-loop | v3 | 2.0 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-024 | entry-point | v3 | 0.2 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-025 | north-grid | v3 | 1.5 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-026 | south-grid | v3 | 2.8 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-027 | hospital-loop | v3 | 1.0 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-028 | entry-point | v4 | 2.3 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-029 | north-grid | v4 | 0.5 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-030 | south-grid | v4 | 1.8 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-031 | hospital-loop | v4 | 0.0 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-032 | entry-point | v4 | 1.3 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-033 | north-grid | v4 | 2.6 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-034 | south-grid | v4 | 0.8 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-035 | hospital-loop | v4 | 2.1 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-036 | entry-point | v4 | 0.3 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-037 | north-grid | v4 | 1.6 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-038 | south-grid | v4 | 2.9 | positive-samples | superseded |\n| LAB-039 | hospital-loop | v4 | 1.1 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-040 | entry-point | v4 | 2.4 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-041 | north-grid | v4 | 0.6 | positive-samples | current |\n\n## Decision constraints\n\nPreserve rounds, spacing, sample count, detection limit, action threshold, and staleness.\nState what negative result would falsify clearance and trigger renewed isolation.\n--- exact batch segment 2 ---\n{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"DELTA\",\"source_path\":\"sources/DELTA_PUMPS.md\",\"source_sha256\":\"4c3707d0d2ae07ceb2bda6d83cf6585510f5398db7c66568ba38aa3fd3f01169\",\"source_size_bytes\":4013,\"start_line\":1}\n--- exact source range ---\n# Pump capacity, sequencing, and cavitation constraints\n\n## Frozen findings\n\nThe treatment works can supply 18 million gallons per day, but the shared transmission main is capped at 14.5 MGD. Pump nameplate capacities cannot be summed into usable system flow.\nThe latest inspected configuration sustained 12.8 MGD after fire-flow and hospital reserve. A higher stage requires a current candidate-bound pump and pressure test.\nRestoration may advance through 10, 30, 60, and 100 percent demand stages only after two thirty-minute windows meet pressure, turbidity, power, and storage gates.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nBASTION supplies pressure limits, ECHO supplies feeder headroom, and FALCON supplies treatment output. All three constrain DELTA sequencing.\nA pump, valve, main allocation, generator, or treatment-train change makes prior capacity evidence stale.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | asset/zone | version | measure | unit | status |\n|---|---|---|---:|---|---|\n| PMP-000 | pump-1 | v2 | 18.0 | million-gallons-day | superseded |\n| PMP-001 | pump-2 | v2 | 19.3 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-002 | booster-east | v2 | 20.6 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-003 | booster-west | v2 | 18.8 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-004 | pump-1 | v2 | 20.1 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-005 | pump-2 | v2 | 18.3 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-006 | booster-east | v2 | 19.6 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-007 | booster-west | v2 | 20.9 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-008 | pump-1 | v2 | 19.1 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-009 | pump-2 | v2 | 20.4 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-010 | booster-east | v2 | 18.6 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-011 | booster-west | v2 | 19.9 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-012 | pump-1 | v2 | 18.1 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-013 | pump-2 | v2 | 19.4 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-014 | booster-east | v3 | 20.7 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-015 | booster-west | v3 | 18.9 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-016 | pump-1 | v3 | 20.2 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-017 | pump-2 | v3 | 18.4 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-018 | booster-east | v3 | 19.7 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-019 | booster-west | v3 | 21.0 | million-gallons-day | superseded |\n| PMP-020 | pump-1 | v3 | 19.2 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-021 | pump-2 | v3 | 20.5 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-022 | booster-east | v3 | 18.7 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-023 | booster-west | v3 | 20.0 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-024 | pump-1 | v3 | 18.2 | million-gallons-day | curre